<title>POLAND: Poland to raise train and bus fares in February.</title>
<headline>Poland to raise train and bus fares in February.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will increase train ticket prices by an average of 11 percent from February 1, 1997, and long-distance bus ticket prices by 10 percent on average, the transport ministry said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to the 1997 budget draft, the February train and bus fare increase will be the last this year.</p>
<p>The government controls prices of the State Railways and PKS long-distance bus operator, which dominate the market.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
